<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102374" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταξῐάρχ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, less common form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταξίαρχος</span>, <i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Fr.</u>
			182.1
		</span></i> (acc. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ας</span>), <i><span class="en">
			Hippod.
		</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
			Stob.
			4.1.94
		</span></i> (nom. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-αι</span>); gen. pl.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έων</span> is v.l. in
		<i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			7.99
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			9.53
		</span></i>, but he uses nom. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταξίαρχοι</span>
		(v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταξίαρχος</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">;
			ταξιαρχῶν</span> is so accented in <i><span class="en">
			Pl.
			<u>Lg.</u>
			755e
		</span></i>, but acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταξιάρχους</span> occurs
		ibid.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ</span>. used as a nickname, <i><span class="en">
			Cic.
			<u>Att.</u>
			16.11.3
		</span></i>; cf. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταξίαρχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.2
				</span></i>
			 and <i><span class="en">
				3b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3c
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
